exports[`audio add-on absent, everything configured > Tome of Lore: each section, opened > Tome of Lore > Lore library 1`] = `
"  [summary "Lore libraryThe notes and documents the AI grounds your chronicle against." open] Lore libraryThe notes and documents the AI grounds your chronicle against.
  Knowledge Base — Tusks-Lore folder
  2 docs · 64 B on disk · 64 B of extracted text. <lore-root>
  [button "Refresh"]
  Drag & drop PDF / DOCX / TXT / MD files here
  or drop them straight into Tusks-Lore in File Explorer, then Refresh.
  [button "Choose files"] [button "Convert one .docx → .md"] [button "Bulk convert .docx in Tusks-Lore"]
  [file-input accept=".pdf,.docx,.txt,.md" multiple] [file-input accept=".docx" multiple]
  Places/Place-Delta.md
  MD · 28 B · 28 chars
  [button "Remove Place-Delta.md"]
  Factions/Faction-Echo.md
  MD · 36 B · 36 chars
  [button "Remove Faction-Echo.md"]
  Lore Index
  Structured metadata extracted from your lore docs. The pipeline uses this for faster lore grounding and cheaper Chronicle calls. Docs without frontmatter still work — they fall back to the proper-noun regex extractor (less precise).
  [button "Refresh"]
  Indexed entities
  2
  With frontmatter
  1
  Without (fallback)
  1
  1 doc lacks structured metadata. The pipeline still works — falls back to a regex proper-noun extractor — but lore retrieval is less precise.
  Factions/Faction-Echo.md
