exports[`audio add-on absent, everything configured > every tab, in order > Help panel 1`] = `
"Help & Documentation
Browse the same docs that live in the GitHub repo, without leaving the app. Each section is collapsible — click to open. Add-on pages link straight here from their settings rows.
[searchbox "Search documentation" value="" placeholder="Search docs by title, path, or topic…" type=search]
Getting started
[button "Quick start docs/getting-started/quick-start.md Documentation."]
Troubleshooting
[button "Diagnostic bundles docs/troubleshooting/diagnostic-bundles.md Diagnostic bundles for a failing run."]
More
[button "Audio transcription docs/modules/audio-transcription.md Documentation."] [button "Tusk’s Tomes README.md Documentation."]
  [summary "About Tusk's Tomes" closed] About Tusk's Tomes
  [img "Tusk's Tomes coat of arms"]
  About Tusk's Tomes
  A chronicler of voyages, deeds, and the things that whisper below — built by a Dungeon Master, for Dungeon Masters and players.
  Why this exists
  ·Local-first, not SaaS. Your transcripts, your keys, your hardware. Audio never leaves the machine; only the text you choose reaches the LLM provider. No account, no telemetry, no rug-pull risk.
  ·AI as scribe, not storyteller. Tusk’s Tomes grounds speakers and lore, writes the chronicle, and surfaces clarifying questions for the DM. It does not invent your session. The story stays yours.
  ·Tools for tables, MIT-licensed. Built for kitchen-table games and small Discord servers. Fork it, modify it, redistribute it — it’s yours, forever free.
  The creator
  Tusk's Tomes is built by [link "@KochiTusker" href="https://github.com/KochiTusker"] — a Dungeon Master who got tired of losing an hour after every session rewriting the recap.
  Contributions, bug reports, and feedback welcome at [link "github.com/KochiTusker/Tusks-Tomes" href="https://github.com/KochiTusker/Tusks-Tomes"] .
  [link "Source GitHub repository" href="https://github.com/KochiTusker/Tusks-Tomes"] [link "License MIT — fully open source" href="https://opensource.org/license/mit/"]
  Version
  0.1.0 — early access
  If Tusk's Tomes saves your session night, you can buy me a coffee.
  [link "Buy me a coffee" href="https://buymeacoffee.com/kochitusker"]
  Tusk's Tomes is MIT-licensed and free to use forever. Donations are entirely optional."
`;

