exports[`audio add-on absent, everything configured > every tab, in order > Settings panel 1`] = `
"Jump to
[button "Providers & models"]
[button "Pipeline tuning"]
[button "Voice & content"]
[button "Transcription"]
[button "Maintenance"]
[searchbox "Search settings" value="" placeholder="Search settings… e.g. api key, persona, whisper" type=search]
New here? Let us set it up for you
Walks through the configuration that works best, and shows you exactly what it will change before changing anything.
[button "Guided setup"]
  [summary "Providers & modelsGemini PaidAPI keys, which provider runs, and what model handles each phase." open] Providers & modelsGemini PaidAPI keys, which provider runs, and what model handles each phase.
  API Keys
  Keys are encrypted at rest and bound to this machine — they cannot be decrypted anywhere else, and they never leave your computer.
  Google Gemini
  The main pipeline needs a billing-enabled Google Cloud key. An optional free-tier key lets the cost-saving presets move the smallest phases off your bill.
  Paid tier (billing-enabled) — primary key, required
  Required for the main pipeline. Supports Gemini 3.x and high-throughput runs.
  Configured
  [button "Test"] [button "Probe models"] [button "Replace"] [button "Clear Paid tier (billing-enabled) — primary key, required"]
  [button "Probed model access(3 accessible)<datetime>" expanded=false]
  Free tier (optional)
  Used by the cost-saving presets for the smallest phases, where free-tier quotas are comfortable. Skip it unless you want that extra saving.
  Not configured
  [button "Add"]
  OpenRouter
  One key, around 400 models from every major vendor — a cheap model for the mechanical phases, a strong one for the prose, without an account for each. Requests only go to hosts that do not retain your prompts; models that cannot meet that bar stay hidden unless you allow them per-model.
  API key
  Configured
  [button "Test"] [button "Replace"] [button "Clear API key"]
    [summary "Claude Code (your subscription)ExperimentalConnectedCLI 1.2.3, signed in." closed] Claude Code (your subscription)ExperimentalConnectedCLI 1.2.3, signed in. [button "Check again"]
    Claude Code (your subscription)
    Uses your own locally-installed Claude Code subscription as the LLM — no API key. Select it as the active provider (or per-phase) once it shows connected below.
    [button "Recheck"]
    CLI installed (1.2.3)Logged in
    Heads up: if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set in your environment it would override your subscription and bill the API. Tusk's Tomes strips it from the CLI call, but it's cleanest to leave it unset. Each user brings their own subscription — this app never handles login.
    [checkbox "Explicit-content failsafeIf Claude Code refuses or blanks a chunk, redo just that chunk on a permissive model mid-run; and after a run where a refusal was detected, offer a pass that reconciles the chronicle against the raw transcript to restore softened or omitted gore, profanity and sexual references. Off by default — ideally never needed." unchecked] Explicit-content failsafeIf Claude Code refuses or blanks a chunk, redo just that chunk on a permissive model mid-run; and after a run where a refusal was detected, offer a pass that reconciles the chronicle against the raw transcript to restore softened or omitted gore, profanity and sexual references. Off by default — ideally never needed.
    [summary "Codex (your ChatGPT subscription)ExperimentalNot foundThe codex CLI was not found on this machine. Install it (npm i -g @openai/codex), run \`codex login\`, then check again." closed] Codex (your ChatGPT subscription)ExperimentalNot foundThe codex CLI was not found on this machine. Install it (npm i -g @openai/codex), run \`codex login\`, then check again. [button "Check again"]
    Uses your own locally-installed OpenAI Codex CLI (ChatGPT Plus/Pro) as a provider — no API key, runs bill against the subscription you already pay for. The app never handles the login.
    Once connected, Codex appears as a subscription option in the plans above and in the per-phase pickers, exactly like Claude Code. If a usage window runs out mid-run, the run pauses itself and resumes at the exact chunk it stopped on.
    Setup: npm i -g @openai/codex, then codex login, then press the refresh arrow on this row. Make sure OPENAI_API_KEY is not set in the environment — it would override the subscription.
    [summary "Local runners — Ollama, LM Studio, UnslothNot foundNo runner answered on the usual ports. Start Ollama, LM Studio or Unsloth Studio, then check again." closed] Local runners — Ollama, LM Studio, UnslothNot foundNo runner answered on the usual ports. Start Ollama, LM Studio or Unsloth Studio, then check again. [button "Check again"]
    Local LLMs
    Detected local backends and their installed models. Run a probe to evaluate eligibility per phase; recommendations below combine probe results with parameter count and your GPU's VRAM.
    [button "Detect again"]
    System
    8 CPUs · CPU-Model-X · 32GB RAM · No NVIDIA GPU detected
    Ollama
    http://localhost:11434
    Offline
    LM Studio
    http://localhost:1234
    Offline
    llama.cpp
    http://localhost:8080
    Offline
    Unsloth Studio
    http://localhost:8888
    Offline
    Unsloth Studio credentials
    Unsloth Studio's API requires auth by default. Provide either a bearer token or username + password (OAuth2 password flow is tried first; HTTP Basic is the fallback). Stored in the same encrypted keystore as the cloud API keys.
    Status: Not configured
    Base URL
    [textbox "Base URL" value="http://localhost:8888" placeholder="http://localhost:8888"]
    Bearer token (optional)
    [textbox "Bearer token (optional)" value=<empty>]
    Username
    [textbox "Username" value="" placeholder="admin"]
    Password
    [textbox "Password" value=<empty>]
    [button "Save"]
    Recommended routing
    Based on the probed capability of each detected local model, its parameter count, and whatever VRAM the legacy Hardware profile reports. Apply via Plan & routing below.
    Phase 1 — GroundingCloudNo local backend detected — every phase routes to cloud.
    Phase 2 — AuditCloudNo local backend detected — every phase routes to cloud.
    Phase 3 — ChronicleCloudNo local backend detected — every phase routes to cloud.
    Phase 4 — ExtrasCloudNo local backend detected — every phase routes to cloud.
    [summary "Plan & routing— Pick a plan, or set each phase's model yourself." open] Plan & routing— Pick a plan, or set each phase's model yourself.
    Gemini Pro everywherebaseline [button "About Gemini Pro everywhere" expanded=false] [button "Apply"]
    The newest top-tier model on all five phases, including the mechanical ones. The yardstick every saving below is measured against.
    Gemini Pro prose + free grounding~40% cheaperestimated [button "About Gemini Pro prose + free grounding" expanded=false] [button "Apply" disabled]
    Chronicle and condense on Gemini Pro; grounding and audit move to Claude Code at no API cost.
    Needs a Gemini key plus the Claude Code or Codex CLI on this machine.
    OpenRouter prose + free grounding~94% cheaperestimated [button "About OpenRouter prose + free grounding" expanded=false] [button "Apply" disabled]
    Chronicle, extras and condense on OpenRouter; grounding and audit on Claude Code at no API cost. No Gemini key needed.
    Needs an OpenRouter key plus the Claude Code or Codex CLI on this machine.
    OpenRouter everywhere~93% cheaperestimated [button "About OpenRouter everywhere" expanded=false] [button "Apply"]
    All five phases on OpenRouter, each on the best model measured for that phase. One key, nothing else.
    Gemini Flash everywhere~77% cheapermeasuredRecommended [button "About Gemini Flash everywhere" expanded=false] [button "Apply"]
    All five phases on the latest Gemini Flash — the configuration that matched Pro in blind testing.
    Claude Code everywhereno API cost [button "About Claude Code everywhere" expanded=false] [button "Apply" disabled]
    All five phases run on Claude Code. No API keys, no per-token cost at all.
    Needs the Claude Code or Codex CLI installed and signed in.
    [checkbox "Show free, small and lower-performing models" unchecked] Show free, small and lower-performing models
    [button "Clear overrides"] [button "Save" disabled]
      [summary "Customise phases— override the model for a single phase; the plans above set the rest." open] Customise phases— override the model for a single phase; the plans above set the rest.
      Each phase defaults to the model your active provider would run. Pick a different option to override a single phase — useful for running cheaper models on simpler phases, or splitting between Gemini Free and Paid to lower costs. Start Ollama, LM Studio or Unsloth and probe it in the Local LLMs panel to route phases to a local model.
      Model lists
      Gemini paid keychecked <relative> ago
      [button "Re-check Gemini paid key"]
      OpenRouterchecked <relative> ago
      [button "Re-check OpenRouter"]
      From openrouter.ai · updates automatically, at most once a day
      [checkbox "Keep the model list up to date automatically" checked] Keep the model list up to date automatically
      GroundOverridden
      Corrects transcription errors against your lore. Near 1:1 in and out.
      Wants: Accuracy and obedience, not flair. The most calls of any phase, so price shows up here.
      [button "gemini-2.5-flashGemini Paid—"]
      $0.214 this phase [button "Reset"]
      AuditInherited
      Reads raw and corrected side by side and asks the DM only what it must.
      Wants: Cheap and terse — it emits almost nothing. No model has been graded on this phase yet.
      [button "gemini-2.5-flashGemini Paid—"]
      $0.066 this phase
      ChronicleOverridden
      Writes the narrative chronicle. Exhaustive, in the table’s own voice.
      Wants: Prose judgement, and tolerance for mature content. Usually most of the bill.
      [button "vendor-a/model-largeOpenRouter—"]
      $0.825 this phase [button "Reset"]
      ExtrasOverridden
      Pulls the quotes, jests and gore worth keeping.
      Wants: A sense of humour and an ear for an exchange. Cheap — output is tiny.
      [button "vendor-b/model-smallOpenRouterC"]
      $0.011 this phase [button "Reset"]
      CondenseInherited
      Condenses the finished chronicle into a recap.
      Wants: Same prose judgement as Chronicle, over a shorter output.
      [button "gemini-2.5-proGemini Paid—"]
      $0.157 this phase
      Model reasoning, per phase
      Gemini phases only. Reasoning on = slower, sharper, ~3× the output cost; off = faster and cheaper. The Chronicle phase always keeps reasoning on. These save immediately.
      [checkbox "Cheaper grounding, same names Phase 1 · turns reasoning off. ~10–15% cheaper — mechanical name-substitution doesn't need it." unchecked]
      Cheaper grounding, same names
      Phase 1 · turns reasoning off. ~10–15% cheaper — mechanical name-substitution doesn't need it.
      [checkbox "Sharper quotes, jests and gore Phase 4 · turns reasoning on. ~3× the extras output cost, but extras are small, so pennies in practice. Worth trying when the quotes feel noisy." unchecked]
      Sharper quotes, jests and gore
      Phase 4 · turns reasoning on. ~3× the extras output cost, but extras are small, so pennies in practice. Worth trying when the quotes feel noisy.
      [checkbox "Condense hits its target length Phase 5 · turns reasoning on. Flash-tier models land the condense target far more reliably — most of Pro's discipline at a fraction of its price." unchecked]
      Condense hits its target length
      Phase 5 · turns reasoning on. Flash-tier models land the condense target far more reliably — most of Pro's discipline at a fraction of its price.
