exports[`audio add-on installed, everything configured > every tab, in order > Sessions panel 1`] = `
"Multitrack audio upload
Upload one or more Craig zips (each becomes one chunk), or one audio file per speaker, or both. Chunks are stitched end-to-end into one session; same speaker across chunks (matched by Craig speaker ID, or by filename for loose files) is merged into one participant. The resulting .sbv interleaves every speaker chronologically. Whisper runs locally — nothing leaves your machine.
Drag & drop files here, or [button "browse"] .
One or more .zip files (one chunk each), and/or loose audio files. Per-file limit: 4 GB. You can upload everything in one batch, or stage parts and commit between batches.
[file-input accept=".zip,.wav,.flac,.ogg,.opus,.mp3,.m4a,.aac,audio/*,application/zip" multiple]
Session label (optional)
[textbox "Session label (optional)" value="" placeholder="e.g. Session 42 — Drow ambush"]
Stored as the session's display name in the Sessions tab. Locked once Part 1 is committed.
How to record a multitrack session
Two paths, both reliable. The Craig path is recommended; you'll split long sessions into chunks (Craig rolls a new recording every hour automatically) and upload them all here.
Option A — Craig bot (chunked)
Invite [link "Craig" href="https://craig.chat"] to your Discord server.
Join your voice channel and run /craig:join. After ~60 minutes, run /craig:leave. Craig DMs you a download link — grab the multi-track FLAC zip.
Immediately rejoin with /craig:join for the next chunk. Repeat until your session is done.
Delete each Craig recording from craig.chat after you've downloaded the zip (their storage is limited).
Drop all the chunk zips onto this page — either all at once, or staged across multiple batches using the Save batch +Add another batch flow. They'll be stitched in upload order (use the ↑/↓ arrows to reorder if needed).
Option B — local per-player recording
Each player records their own mic locally (Audacity, OBS, Windows Voice Recorder). Name the file with the player's name, e.g. Wyldfyre.wav.
Everyone hits Record at "3, 2, 1, go" on Discord so the tracks share a start time.
Collect all files in a folder, drag-drop them all here at once. They form one chunk.
Staged batch uploads
Got 12 GB of Craig zips and a flaky internet connection? Drop the first few zips, click Save Part 1, wait for the green confirmation, then click Add another batch for the next set. Each batch commits independently — if Part 3 fails upload, Parts 1 and 2 stay saved and you can retry just Part 3. When everything's uploaded, click the green All audio uploaded — start transcription button. Whisper runs once across the whole stitched session.
Uploaded sessions
Multitrack uploads on disk. Click Process to transcribe with Whisper and emit a speaker-tagged SBV, then send it into the refinement flow.
[button "Refresh"]
Table
<datetime> · 1 participant · 1 utterance · 4h 3m
Processed
[button "View transcript" expanded=false] [link "Download SBV" href="/api/sessions/aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/sbv"] [button "Send to Refinement"] [button "Delete audio (keep transcript)"] [button "Delete session"]"
`;

