exports[`audio add-on installed, everything configured > every tab, in order > Settings panel 1`] = `
"Jump to
[button "Providers & models"]
[button "Pipeline tuning"]
[button "Voice & content"]
[button "Transcription"]
[button "Maintenance"]
[searchbox "Search settings" value="" placeholder="Search settings… e.g. api key, persona, whisper" type=search]
New here? Let us set it up for you
Walks through the configuration that works best, and shows you exactly what it will change before changing anything.
[button "Guided setup"]
  [summary "Providers & modelsGemini PaidAPI keys, which provider runs, and what model handles each phase." open] Providers & modelsGemini PaidAPI keys, which provider runs, and what model handles each phase.
  API Keys
  Keys are encrypted at rest and bound to this machine — they cannot be decrypted anywhere else, and they never leave your computer.
  Google Gemini
  The main pipeline needs a billing-enabled Google Cloud key. An optional free-tier key lets the cost-saving presets move the smallest phases off your bill.
  Paid tier (billing-enabled) — primary key, required
  Required for the main pipeline. Supports Gemini 3.x and high-throughput runs.
  Configured
  [button "Test"] [button "Probe models"] [button "Replace"] [button "Clear Paid tier (billing-enabled) — primary key, required"]
  [button "Probed model access(3 accessible)<datetime>" expanded=false]
  Free tier (optional)
  Used by the cost-saving presets for the smallest phases, where free-tier quotas are comfortable. Skip it unless you want that extra saving.
  Not configured
  [button "Add"]
  OpenRouter
  One key, around 400 models from every major vendor — a cheap model for the mechanical phases, a strong one for the prose, without an account for each. Requests only go to hosts that do not retain your prompts; models that cannot meet that bar stay hidden unless you allow them per-model.
  API key
  Configured
  [button "Test"] [button "Replace"] [button "Clear API key"]
    [summary "Claude Code (your subscription)ExperimentalConnectedCLI 1.2.3, signed in." closed] Claude Code (your subscription)ExperimentalConnectedCLI 1.2.3, signed in. [button "Check again"]
    Claude Code (your subscription)
    Uses your own locally-installed Claude Code subscription as the LLM — no API key. Select it as the active provider (or per-phase) once it shows connected below.
    [button "Recheck"]
    CLI installed (1.2.3)Logged in
    Heads up: if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set in your environment it would override your subscription and bill the API. Tusk's Tomes strips it from the CLI call, but it's cleanest to leave it unset. Each user brings their own subscription — this app never handles login.
    [checkbox "Explicit-content failsafeIf Claude Code refuses or blanks a chunk, redo just that chunk on a permissive model mid-run; and after a run where a refusal was detected, offer a pass that reconciles the chronicle against the raw transcript to restore softened or omitted gore, profanity and sexual references. Off by default — ideally never needed." unchecked] Explicit-content failsafeIf Claude Code refuses or blanks a chunk, redo just that chunk on a permissive model mid-run; and after a run where a refusal was detected, offer a pass that reconciles the chronicle against the raw transcript to restore softened or omitted gore, profanity and sexual references. Off by default — ideally never needed.
    [summary "Codex (your ChatGPT subscription)ExperimentalNot foundThe codex CLI was not found on this machine. Install it (npm i -g @openai/codex), run \`codex login\`, then check again." closed] Codex (your ChatGPT subscription)ExperimentalNot foundThe codex CLI was not found on this machine. Install it (npm i -g @openai/codex), run \`codex login\`, then check again. [button "Check again"]
    Uses your own locally-installed OpenAI Codex CLI (ChatGPT Plus/Pro) as a provider — no API key, runs bill against the subscription you already pay for. The app never handles the login.
    Once connected, Codex appears as a subscription option in the plans above and in the per-phase pickers, exactly like Claude Code. If a usage window runs out mid-run, the run pauses itself and resumes at the exact chunk it stopped on.
    Setup: npm i -g @openai/codex, then codex login, then press the refresh arrow on this row. Make sure OPENAI_API_KEY is not set in the environment — it would override the subscription.
    [summary "Local runners — Ollama, LM Studio, UnslothNot foundNo runner answered on the usual ports. Start Ollama, LM Studio or Unsloth Studio, then check again." closed] Local runners — Ollama, LM Studio, UnslothNot foundNo runner answered on the usual ports. Start Ollama, LM Studio or Unsloth Studio, then check again. [button "Check again"]
