      Sharper quotes, jests and gore
      Phase 4 · turns reasoning on. ~3× the extras output cost, but extras are small, so pennies in practice. Worth trying when the quotes feel noisy.
      [checkbox "Condense hits its target length Phase 5 · turns reasoning on. Flash-tier models land the condense target far more reliably — most of Pro's discipline at a fraction of its price." unchecked]
      Condense hits its target length
      Phase 5 · turns reasoning on. Flash-tier models land the condense target far more reliably — most of Pro's discipline at a fraction of its price.
      Overrides saved. [button "Save" disabled]
    [summary "Browse OpenRouter models— Prices, grades and policies for the whole catalogue. Reference only: pick phase models in the routing rows above." open] Browse OpenRouter models— Prices, grades and policies for the whole catalogue. Reference only: pick phase models in the routing rows above.
    The catalogue [button "Refresh"]
    3 models, priced live. Fetched <datetime>. Cost is for one 3-hour session, 10,000 words of lore.
    Grades are quality only — price is the column beside them [button "How these are decided" expanded=false]
    ADoes this phase well. Nothing measured does it better.BSolid, with small shortfalls you would notice if you looked for them.CNoticeably weak at this phase, though the output is usable.DFails the phase's core contract. Only with output checks.FCannot run this phase, or fails it outright.—Not measured yet. Unknown, not assumed good or bad.
    B?A dashed chip was not measured on this model, and it is one of two things. A prediction is read off the model's purpose or its declared size, with no run behind it anywhere; a prediction never awards an A, because only a real comparison can show something beating the reference. An inherited grade did come from a real run, on another version or channel of the same tier, so it keeps whatever letter that run earned. Both exist so that a 400-model catalogue can be narrowed at all; running every model would cost more than the tool saves. Expand a row to read which one it is and what it was based on, and tick Tested by the maintainer to see only models that have genuinely been run here. Reviewed 2026-08-27.
    [textbox value="" placeholder="Filter by name, e.g. deepseek"]
    [combobox value="Cheapest first" options=["Cheapest first","Largest context first","Name"]]
    [checkbox "Show free models" unchecked] Show free models
    [checkbox "Show lower-performing and small models" unchecked] Show lower-performing and small models
    [checkbox "Handles mature content(21)" unchecked] Handles mature content(21)
    [checkbox "Tested by the maintainer(19)" unchecked] Tested by the maintainer(19)
    [button "vendor-b/model-smallhas content filter ~$0.09 / sessionin $0.100 · out $0.400 per Mctx 128kmax out 16k Overall C?|Ground C?Audit C?Chronicle C?Extras C?Condense C? predicted only"]
    [button "vendor-a/model-large ~$3.08 / sessionin $3.00 · out $15.00 per Mctx 200kmax out 64k Overall —|Ground —Audit —Chronicle —Extras —Condense — untested"]
  [summary "Pipeline tuningOptional quality and cost adjustments. All default to off." open] Pipeline tuningOptional quality and cost adjustments. All default to off.
  Pipeline tuning
  Optional adjustments to output quality and cost. Every one defaults to off — your runs behave exactly as they do today until you change something here.
  [checkbox "Send only relevant lore to Chronicle and Condense−92% lore sentBoth steps receive just the notes your session mentions, instead of your whole vault." unchecked] Send only relevant lore to Chronicle and Condense−92% lore sent [button "About lore retrieval" expanded=false] Both steps receive just the notes your session mentions, instead of your whole vault.
  [checkbox "Reassemble fragmented quotesquotes 70% → 93% completeLets the Extras phase rejoin split speech into complete sentences before quoting it." unchecked] Reassemble fragmented quotesquotes 70% → 93% complete [button "About quote reassembly" expanded=false] Lets the Extras phase rejoin split speech into complete sentences before quoting it.
  [checkbox "Use lore aliases to catch misheard namesno extra costGrounding gets phonetic hints from your lore index, for names transcription mangles." unchecked] Use lore aliases to catch misheard namesno extra cost [button "About alias hints" expanded=false] Grounding gets phonetic hints from your lore index, for names transcription mangles.
  [summary "Voice & contentThe voice your chronicle is written in, and what the models may filter." open] Voice & contentThe voice your chronicle is written in, and what the models may filter.
  Chronicle Personas
  Switch the Chronicle narrator out of the locked Bard default. The Bard prompt is always available and cannot be edited; personas defined here override phases 3, 3.5, and 5 when selected from the Chronicle tab dropdown.
  [button "From preset"] [button "From template"] [button "From scratch"] [button "Generate with AI"]
  Presets
  Persona-OnePreset
  A gruff narrator preset.
  [button "Edit"] [button "Delete"]
  Persona-TwoPreset
  A wry narrator preset.
  [button "Edit"] [button "Delete"]
  Custom
  Persona-Custom
  Authored by the user.
  [button "Edit"] [button "Delete"]
  Guardrails
  All off — model responses are unfiltered.
  [button "Adjust"]
  [summary "TranscriptionInstalledTurning recorded audio into a transcript — the one feature that installs." open] TranscriptionInstalledTurning recorded audio into a transcript — the one feature that installs.
  Add-ons
  Features that put real bytes on disk live here. Everything else — personas, local runners, the CLI bridges, the Obsidian lore source — is part of the app and configured from its own panel.
  Audio TranscriptionEnabled
  Whisper sidecar and the Sessions tab.
  [button "Read docs"]
  [switch "On" checked] On
  [button "Uninstall"]
  Whisper Audio TranscriptionInstalled
  Whisper is ready. Upload Craig recordings from the Sessions tab and transcribe them locally.
  [button "Read the Audio Transcription docs"]
  [button "Uninstall"]
    [summary "whisper.cpp bridge (your own build)ExperimentalNot foundNot set up — no binary or model paths saved yet. Point the panel at your whisper.cpp build and a model file." open] whisper.cpp bridge (your own build)ExperimentalNot foundNot set up — no binary or model paths saved yet. Point the panel at your whisper.cpp build and a model file. [button "Check again"]
    whisper.cpp bridge [button "About the whisper.cpp bridge" expanded=false]
    Not set up
    Checking…
    Path to the whisper.cpp executable
    [textbox "Path to the whisper.cpp executable" value="" placeholder="C:\\\\dev\\\\whisper.cpp\\\\build\\\\bin\\\\Release\\\\whisper-cli.exe"]
    Path to the GGML model file
    [textbox "Path to the GGML model file" value="" placeholder="C:\\\\dev\\\\whisper.cpp\\\\models\\\\ggml-large-v3.bin"]
    Both must be full paths. Anything under 20 MB is rejected — that's almost always a Git-LFS pointer rather than the real weights.
    [button "Save and check" disabled] [button "Re-check"]
    While this is set up and working, audio transcription uses whisper.cpp instead of the built-in engine. If anything here stops checking out, it falls back automatically rather than failing your run.
  [summary "MaintenanceUpdates, diagnostics, and developer tools." open] MaintenanceUpdates, diagnostics, and developer tools.
  Updates
  Pull the latest main from GitHub. Runs git pull on your disk and refuses to clobber uncommitted local edits. npm install only runs when the pulled commits actually touch package.json or package-lock.json — most updates skip it and complete in a second or two.
  [button "Check for updates"]
  BranchmainCurrent0000000 — Release vXorigin/main0000000 — Release vXLast fetchnever
  You're on the latest version.
  Diagnostics
  Opt-in event + error logging for debugging. Three independent output channels: the browser console (F12), the dev-server terminal wherenpm run dev runs, and a JSON Lines log file on disk. Ring buffer (last 500 entries) fills regardless of toggles, so you can flip channels on AFTER a bug happens and still copy the recent history below.
  [checkbox "Verbose console logging (browser)Streams each event to F12 → Console with a category tag (e.g. [tusk:gemini]). Most lightweight option — no network, no disk." unchecked]
  Verbose console logging (browser)Streams each event to F12 → Console with a category tag (e.g. [tusk:gemini]). Most lightweight option — no network, no disk.
  [checkbox "Forward to dev-server terminalStreams each event to the Node terminal wherenpm run devis running. Pretty-printed with ANSI colors, one line per event. Best for live observation while you scroll the terminal back. Sanitized before send — fields named apiKey,userPrompt, etc. become[REDACTED] (lengths preserved as<field>_chars)." unchecked]
  Forward to dev-server terminalStreams each event to the Node terminal wherenpm run devis running. Pretty-printed with ANSI colors, one line per event. Best for live observation while you scroll the terminal back. Sanitized before send — fields named apiKey,userPrompt, etc. become[REDACTED] (lengths preserved as<field>_chars).
  [checkbox "Also write to diagnostics.logAppends each event as JSON Lines to a file in your platform config directory (grep / jq friendly for forensics). Survives browser reload. File grows until cleared via the button below." unchecked]
  Also write to diagnostics.logAppends each event as JSON Lines to a file in your platform config directory (grep / jq friendly for forensics). Survives browser reload. File grows until cleared via the button below.
  [checkbox "Persist blocked-chunk text to .diagnose/blocked-chunks/When Gemini's unconfigurable filter (PROHIBITED_CONTENT / BLOCKLIST / SPII) rejects a Phase 2 or Phase 4 chunk, capture the FULL prompt body (including your transcript text) to disk so you can inspect exactly what content the model classified as forbidden. Off by default — opt in only when you're actively investigating, since this writes user transcript content to the repo's gitignored.diagnose/blocked-chunks/ directory." unchecked]
  Persist blocked-chunk text to .diagnose/blocked-chunks/When Gemini's unconfigurable filter (PROHIBITED_CONTENT / BLOCKLIST / SPII) rejects a Phase 2 or Phase 4 chunk, capture the FULL prompt body (including your transcript text) to disk so you can inspect exactly what content the model classified as forbidden. Off by default — opt in only when you're actively investigating, since this writes user transcript content to the repo's gitignored.diagnose/blocked-chunks/ directory.
  Log file
  <log-dir>/diagnostics.log [button "Copy path"] [button "Clear log file"]
  On POSIX: tail -f <log-dir>/diagnostics.log to follow live, or cat <log-dir>/diagnostics.log | jq 'select(.cat=="gemini")' to filter.
  Browser ring buffer
  [combobox "Filter log entries by category" value="All categories" options=["All categories","pipeline","chunk","provider","gemini","sessions","routing","refresh","fallback","cache","resume"]] [button "Copy to clipboard"] [button "Clear buffer"] [button "Show server ring"]
  Pastes well into a bug report or Claude Code session — each line is [HH:mm:ss.sss] [category] {...JSON...}. The "Show server ring" button pulls the merged browser+server timeline so you can see what the server logged interleaved with the browser events.
  Diagnosis bundles for Claude Code
  [button "Build bundle now"]
  Auto-builds whenever a pipeline error fires. Writes a structured markdown file at .diagnose/latest.md containing current state, soft-error signatures, last 80 ring events, graphify slice of the throw site, probe cache snapshot, routing.json, and git state. Paste @.diagnose/latest.md into Claude Code for one-round-trip diagnosis.
  Recent bundles (1)
  bundle-1.md2.0 kB<datetime> [button "Copy path to bundle-1.md"]
    [summary "DevTools console reference" open] DevTools console reference
    Type these in the F12 console for direct access to the same ring buffer the panel above reads from:
    // Browser console stream window.__tusk.setVerbose(true) window.__tusk.setVerbose(false) window.__tusk.isVerbose() // Dev-server terminal stream window.__tusk.setTerminalForwarding(true) window.__tusk.isTerminalForwarding() // Disk JSON Lines log window.__tusk.setFileLogging(true) window.__tusk.isFileLogging() // Read recent events window.__tusk.dumpRecentEvents() // last 100 (browser-local) window.__tusk.dumpRecentEvents({ count: 500 }) window.__tusk.dumpRecentEvents({ cat: 'gemini' }) window.__tusk.recentFromServer().then(console.table) // merged server ring window.__tusk.recentFromServer({ cat: 'gemini' }).then(console.table) window.__tusk.clearLog() // wipe browser ring"
`;

exports[`audio add-on installed, everything configured > every tab, in order > Tome of Lore panel 1`] = `
"Jump to
[button "Lore source"]
[button "Names & corrections"]
  [summary "Lore sourceTusks-Lore folderWhere your canon is read from, and the notes it contains.5" closed] Lore sourceTusks-Lore folderWhere your canon is read from, and the notes it contains.5
  Lore Source
  Choose which source grounds your chronicles. Everything below reflects the active source. Configure the vault path, readiness, and Mode-B in Settings → Obsidian Vault Lore.
  [radio "Tusks-Lore folder" checked=true] [radio "Obsidian vault" checked=false]
  Active: Tusks-Lore folder. Your Obsidian vault is configured but not in use.
  Obsidian Vault Lore (read-only)Experimental
  Ground chronicles against an Obsidian vault instead of the Tusks-Lore folder. The app reads your notes' frontmatter aliases + bodies — it never writes into the vault (except the explicit "Build graphify map" action below). Off by default.
  [button "Refresh"]
  Vault path
  [textbox "Vault path Browse…" value="" placeholder="e.g. D:\\\\\\\\Obsidian or ~/Vault"] [button "Browse…"]
  Vault not foundno entity-index (will walk notes)
  [checkbox "Use this vault as the lore sourceWhen on, grounding + the chronicle Knowledge Base come from the vault instead of Tusks-Lore. When off, Tusks-Lore is used (unchanged)." unchecked] Use this vault as the lore sourceWhen on, grounding + the chronicle Knowledge Base come from the vault instead of Tusks-Lore. When off, Tusks-Lore is used (unchanged).
  [checkbox "Relationship enrichment (Mode-B)Prepend each note with a one-line summary of its frontmatter relationships (affiliations, related, patron, allies/enemies) so the chronicle has richer context." unchecked] Relationship enrichment (Mode-B)Prepend each note with a one-line summary of its frontmatter relationships (affiliations, related, patron, allies/enemies) so the chronicle has richer context.
  [checkbox "Use the vault's CLAUDE.md as grounding contextOff by default. When on, your vault's CLAUDE.md navigation guide is injected as a bounded context block so grounding understands how your lore is organised. Changes grounding output — leave off unless you've tuned a CLAUDE.md for this.No CLAUDE.md in this vault yet — generate one from the Tome of Lore tab (needs the Claude Code add-on) or add your own. Until then this toggle has no effect." unchecked] Use the vault's CLAUDE.md as grounding contextOff by default. When on, your vault's CLAUDE.md navigation guide is injected as a bounded context block so grounding understands how your lore is organised. Changes grounding output — leave off unless you've tuned a CLAUDE.md for this.No CLAUDE.md in this vault yet — generate one from the Tome of Lore tab (needs the Claude Code add-on) or add your own. Until then this toggle has no effect.
  [button "Save"] [button "Reindex vault" disabled]
  Get the most out of your vault
  The single highest-value field is aliases: in each note's frontmatter — list nicknames / alternate spellings so grounding can map them to canonical names.
  One note per entity, with a type: (npc, pc, location, faction, deity…).
  Recommended plugins are shown above with live status (read from your vault's enabled-plugins list).
  Tusk's Lore — shared lore base
  A sibling folder both Tusk's Tomes and Tusk's Vault read from. Tomes saves finished chronicles into Tusks-Lore/Sessions/ as structured .docx files; Vault treats the same folder as a lore corpus for in-Discord retrieval. Drop the folder as a sibling of this repo (e.g. Documents/Tusks-Lore/) and it gets auto-detected on next start.
  [button "Re-detect Tusk's Lore"]
  Tusk's Lore detected (sibling directory).
  Lore root
  <lore-root>
  Sessions folder
  <lore-root>/Sessions
  Existing sessions
  2 .docx files
  Writable
  yes
  On a finished chronicle, hit Save to Tusk's Lore to writeTusks-Lore/Sessions/<campaign>/Session-NN-<date>-<full|condensed>.docx.
  Paired with Tusk's Vault
  Tusk's Vault is the sister project — a NotebookLM-style lore assistant for your campaign that lives in your Discord. If you install it as a sibling directory to this repo, finished chronicles can be pushed into Vault's Lore folder with one click and Vault will cite them when players ask in-game questions. [link "View Tusk's Vault on GitHub" href="https://github.com/KochiTusker/Tusks-Vault"]
  [button "Re-detect Tusk's Vault"]
  Vault not detected.
  Pair the projects by installing the Vault repo as a sibling directory of this one — e.g. if Tomes is at~/Tusks-Tomes(or C:/Users/<you>/Tusks-Tomes on Windows), clone Vault to ~/Tusks-Vault. Or set TUSKS_VAULT_DIR in .env to point at your Vault checkout if it lives somewhere else.
  • Sister project not found.
    [summary "Lore libraryThe notes and documents the AI grounds your chronicle against.2" closed] Lore libraryThe notes and documents the AI grounds your chronicle against.2
    Knowledge Base — Tusks-Lore folder
    2 docs · 64 B on disk · 64 B of extracted text. <lore-root>
    [button "Refresh"]
    Drag & drop PDF / DOCX / TXT / MD files here
    or drop them straight into Tusks-Lore in File Explorer, then Refresh.
    [button "Choose files"] [button "Convert one .docx → .md"] [button "Bulk convert .docx in Tusks-Lore"]
    [file-input accept=".pdf,.docx,.txt,.md" multiple] [file-input accept=".docx" multiple]
    Places/Place-Delta.md
    MD · 28 B · 28 chars
    [button "Remove Place-Delta.md"]
    Factions/Faction-Echo.md
    MD · 36 B · 36 chars
    [button "Remove Faction-Echo.md"]
    Lore Index
    Structured metadata extracted from your lore docs. The pipeline uses this for faster lore grounding and cheaper Chronicle calls. Docs without frontmatter still work — they fall back to the proper-noun regex extractor (less precise).
    [button "Refresh"]
    Indexed entities
    2
    With frontmatter
    1
    Without (fallback)
    1
    1 doc lacks structured metadata. The pipeline still works — falls back to a regex proper-noun extractor — but lore retrieval is less precise.
    Factions/Faction-Echo.md
    [link "Download lore template" href="/api/lore/template"] [button "Preview proposed frontmatter"]
  [summary "Names & correctionsFix names transcription mishears, and map speakers to characters." open] Names & correctionsFix names transcription mishears, and map speakers to characters.
  Glossary
  Campaign-specific corrections applied during grounding. Safe replacements run deterministically before any AI call; contextual hints are injected into the AI prompt for case-by-case judgement.
  [button "Save" disabled]
  Safe Replacements
  Unambiguous fixes. The wrong form is never a real word. Matched case-insensitively as a whole word.
  [button "Add rule"]
  [textbox value="delter" placeholder="from (mistranscription)"] → [textbox value="Place-Delta" placeholder="to (canonical)"] [button "Remove rule"]
  [textbox value="echo guild" placeholder="from (mistranscription)"] → [textbox value="Faction-Echo" placeholder="to (canonical)"] [button "Remove rule"]
  Contextual Hints
  For cases where the wrong form IS a real word. The AI decides per-occurrence based on your notes.
  [button "Add hint"]
  Canonical
  [textbox "Canonical" value="PC-Alpha" placeholder="e.g. Az"]
  Common mishears (comma separated)
  [textbox "Common mishears (comma separated)" value="alpha" placeholder="as, Asz, Aza"]
  [button "Remove hint"]
  Notes (when to apply)
  [textbox "Notes (when to apply)" value="The first player character." placeholder="REPLACE only when …; DO NOT REPLACE when …"]
  Speakers
  Map speaker IDs to player and character names. When you upload a Craig zip the speaker IDs are populated automatically from the per-track filenames; you fill in the player and character names. The transcriber uses this to tag each line with the speaker.
  [button "Save" disabled]
  [button "Add speaker"]
  Track: Handle-One
  [button "Remove speaker"]
  Speaker ID
  [textbox "Speaker ID" value="speaker-1" placeholder="Craig speaker ID or any unique handle"]
  Track display name
  [textbox "Track display name" value="Handle-One" placeholder="wyldfyre_dm"]
  Player name
  [textbox "Player name" value="Player-One" placeholder="Wyldfyre"]
  Character name
  [textbox "Character name" value="PC-Alpha" placeholder="Ottilie"]
  Track: Handle-Two
  [button "Remove speaker"]
  Speaker ID
  [textbox "Speaker ID" value="speaker-2" placeholder="Craig speaker ID or any unique handle"]
  Track display name
  [textbox "Track display name" value="Handle-Two" placeholder="wyldfyre_dm"]
  Player name
  [textbox "Player name" value="Player-Two" placeholder="Wyldfyre"]
  Character name
  [textbox "Character name" value="PC-Bravo" placeholder="Ottilie"]"
`;

