exports[`first run: no keys, no audio, no content > every tab, in order > Tome of Lore panel 1`] = `
"Jump to
[button "Lore source"]
[button "Names & corrections"]
  [summary "Lore sourceTusks-Lore folderWhere your canon is read from, and the notes it contains.5" closed] Lore sourceTusks-Lore folderWhere your canon is read from, and the notes it contains.5
  Lore Source
  Choose which source grounds your chronicles. Everything below reflects the active source. Configure the vault path, readiness, and Mode-B in Settings → Obsidian Vault Lore.
  [radio "Tusks-Lore folder" checked=true] [radio "Obsidian vault" checked=false]
  Active: Tusks-Lore folder. Your Obsidian vault is configured but not in use.
  Obsidian Vault Lore (read-only)Experimental
  Ground chronicles against an Obsidian vault instead of the Tusks-Lore folder. The app reads your notes' frontmatter aliases + bodies — it never writes into the vault (except the explicit "Build graphify map" action below). Off by default.
  [button "Refresh"]
  Vault path
  [textbox "Vault path Browse…" value="" placeholder="e.g. D:\\\\\\\\Obsidian or ~/Vault"] [button "Browse…"]
  Vault not foundno entity-index (will walk notes)
  [checkbox "Use this vault as the lore sourceWhen on, grounding + the chronicle Knowledge Base come from the vault instead of Tusks-Lore. When off, Tusks-Lore is used (unchanged)." unchecked] Use this vault as the lore sourceWhen on, grounding + the chronicle Knowledge Base come from the vault instead of Tusks-Lore. When off, Tusks-Lore is used (unchanged).
  [checkbox "Relationship enrichment (Mode-B)Prepend each note with a one-line summary of its frontmatter relationships (affiliations, related, patron, allies/enemies) so the chronicle has richer context." unchecked] Relationship enrichment (Mode-B)Prepend each note with a one-line summary of its frontmatter relationships (affiliations, related, patron, allies/enemies) so the chronicle has richer context.
  [checkbox "Use the vault's CLAUDE.md as grounding contextOff by default. When on, your vault's CLAUDE.md navigation guide is injected as a bounded context block so grounding understands how your lore is organised. Changes grounding output — leave off unless you've tuned a CLAUDE.md for this.No CLAUDE.md in this vault yet — generate one from the Tome of Lore tab (needs the Claude Code add-on) or add your own. Until then this toggle has no effect." unchecked] Use the vault's CLAUDE.md as grounding contextOff by default. When on, your vault's CLAUDE.md navigation guide is injected as a bounded context block so grounding understands how your lore is organised. Changes grounding output — leave off unless you've tuned a CLAUDE.md for this.No CLAUDE.md in this vault yet — generate one from the Tome of Lore tab (needs the Claude Code add-on) or add your own. Until then this toggle has no effect.
  [button "Save"] [button "Reindex vault" disabled]
  Get the most out of your vault
  The single highest-value field is aliases: in each note's frontmatter — list nicknames / alternate spellings so grounding can map them to canonical names.
  One note per entity, with a type: (npc, pc, location, faction, deity…).
  Recommended plugins are shown above with live status (read from your vault's enabled-plugins list).
  Tusk's Lore — shared lore base
  A sibling folder both Tusk's Tomes and Tusk's Vault read from. Tomes saves finished chronicles into Tusks-Lore/Sessions/ as structured .docx files; Vault treats the same folder as a lore corpus for in-Discord retrieval. Drop the folder as a sibling of this repo (e.g. Documents/Tusks-Lore/) and it gets auto-detected on next start.
  [button "Re-detect Tusk's Lore"]
  Tusk's Lore not detected.
  Click below and Tomes will create <default-lore-path> with a marker file plus an empty Sessions/ subfolder. Vault auto-detects the same folder once it's there.
  • No lore folder found.
  [button "Create Tusk's Lore"]
  Paired with Tusk's Vault
  Tusk's Vault is the sister project — a NotebookLM-style lore assistant for your campaign that lives in your Discord. If you install it as a sibling directory to this repo, finished chronicles can be pushed into Vault's Lore folder with one click and Vault will cite them when players ask in-game questions. [link "View Tusk's Vault on GitHub" href="https://github.com/KochiTusker/Tusks-Vault"]
  [button "Re-detect Tusk's Vault"]
  Vault not detected.
  Pair the projects by installing the Vault repo as a sibling directory of this one — e.g. if Tomes is at~/Tusks-Tomes(or C:/Users/<you>/Tusks-Tomes on Windows), clone Vault to ~/Tusks-Vault. Or set TUSKS_VAULT_DIR in .env to point at your Vault checkout if it lives somewhere else.
  • Sister project not found.
    [summary "Lore libraryThe notes and documents the AI grounds your chronicle against.2" closed] Lore libraryThe notes and documents the AI grounds your chronicle against.2
    Knowledge Base — Tusks-Lore folder
    Tusks-Lore folder not detected. Create it from Settings, then refresh.
    [button "Refresh"]
    No lore folder found next to the app.
    Drag & drop PDF / DOCX / TXT / MD files here
    or drop them straight into Tusks-Lore in File Explorer, then Refresh.
    [button "Choose files" disabled] [button "Convert one .docx → .md"] [button "Bulk convert .docx in Tusks-Lore" disabled]
    [file-input accept=".pdf,.docx,.txt,.md" multiple] [file-input accept=".docx" multiple]
    No lore loaded.
  [summary "Names & correctionsFix names transcription mishears, and map speakers to characters." open] Names & correctionsFix names transcription mishears, and map speakers to characters.
  Glossary
  Campaign-specific corrections applied during grounding. Safe replacements run deterministically before any AI call; contextual hints are injected into the AI prompt for case-by-case judgement.
  [button "Save" disabled]
  Safe Replacements
  Unambiguous fixes. The wrong form is never a real word. Matched case-insensitively as a whole word.
  [button "Add rule"]
  No safe replacements. Add one to start.
  Contextual Hints
  For cases where the wrong form IS a real word. The AI decides per-occurrence based on your notes.
  [button "Add hint"]
  No contextual hints yet.
  Speakers
  Map speaker IDs to player and character names. When you upload a Craig zip the speaker IDs are populated automatically from the per-track filenames; you fill in the player and character names. The transcriber uses this to tag each line with the speaker.
  [button "Save" disabled]
  [button "Add speaker"]
  No speakers yet. Upload a Craig multitrack zip via the Sessions tab to auto-populate this list, or add rows manually."
`;

